==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{der|en|frm|-}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|reverse|ible}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹəˈvɜː(ɹ)sɪbəl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-reversible.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Able to be [[reverse]]d.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=June|title=Talking of Trains: Sunday on the G.N. line|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=322|text=[...] the Welwyn bottleneck will be relaid with high-speed turnouts and resignalled for '''reversible''' working.}}
# {{lb|en|of|clothing}} Able to be [[worn]] [[inside out]].
# (''[[chemistry]], of a [[chemical reaction]]'') Capable of proceeding in either [[direction]].
# {{lb|en|physics|of a phase change}} Capable of returning to the [[original]] [[state]].
# {{lb|en|thermodynamics}} Capable of returning to the original state without consumption of free energy and increase of [[entropy]].
# {{lb|en|law}} Providing sufficient reason for a court decision to be [[overturn]]ed on [[appeal]].

